 service as an independently owned, independently stored distributed)Tj T* (system.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 48.51969 633.7969 cm .12549 .14902 .180392 rg BT 12.2 TL/F2+0 8.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3.5 Tm (Two supporting patterns are deliberately part of this decision:)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 48.51969 593.9969 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 14.4 TL/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 9 22.8 Tm <7f>Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 61.51969 593.9969 cm .12549 .14902 .180392 rg BT 11.6 TL/F2+0 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 13 26.3 Tm (Repository / relational transaction boundary: PostgreSQL is the source of truth for rides, join requests, fare)Tj T* (calculations, accounts, and audit data. )Tj/F3+0 8.5 Tf (SELECT FOR UPDATE)Tj/F2+0 8.5 Tf (, validation, related updates, and)Tj T* (commit/rollback protect the seat-allocation path.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 48.51969 556.1969 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 14.4 TL/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 9 22.8 Tm <7f>Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 61.51969 556.1969 cm .12549 .14902 .180392 rg BT -.022529 Tw 11.6 TL/F2+0 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 13 26.3 Tm (Event-driven pub/sub for notifications only: services publish ride, join, and chat state changes to an event bus;)Tj T* 0 Tw (push and email consumers distribute them. This decouples notification delivery from the completed)Tj T* (transaction without moving ownership of the transaction itself into the event stream.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 48.51969 538.1969 cm .090196 .196078 .301961 rg BT 13 TL/F3+0 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 2.8 Tm (3.2 Why this is the best fit)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 48.51969 486.3969 cm .12549 .14902 .180392 rg BT 12.2 TL/F2+0 8.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 40.1 Tm (It keeps the boundary between browser, application, and data concerns easy to understand and test for a)Tj T* (semester project while satisfying the hard parts of the domain: role authorization, ACID updates, row-level)Tj T* (contention, audit records, and real-time client notification. A central API gateway also provides one place to)Tj T* (enforce authentication and route both ordinary API calls and AI requests to their appropriate policy boundaries.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 48.51969 432.5969 cm .12549 .14902 .180392 rg BT 12.2 TL/F2+0 8.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 40.1 Tm (The architecture is intentionally central rather than device-distributed. The workload is modest \(the requirements)Tj T* (describe at least 100 daily active users and 250 core transactions per day\), but correctness when a seat is)Tj T* (accepted is non-negotiable. A shared relational store and a single transactional service boundary make that)Tj T* (correctness much more direct to implement and verify.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 1 1 rg 1 1 1 RG 40.51969 16.11285 514.2368 11.20001 re B Q q Q q Q
