T* (context assembly, output validation,)Tj T* (deterministic graceful degradation)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 344.1575 75.7 cm .12549 .14902 .180392 rg BT 9.1 TL/F2+0 7.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 56.6 Tm (The agent invokes only allowlisted read tools)Tj T* (\(and may propose, but not apply, a)Tj T* (preference change\). It ranks/explains rides)Tj T* (and interprets natural language. The system)Tj T* (validates every displayed identifier and fact.)Tj T* (The rider, not the agent, takes any)Tj T* (consequential action.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 4 58.6 cm .12549 .14902 .180392 rg BT 9.1 TL/F2+0 7.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 2 Tm (Operations Admin complaint analysis)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 174.0787 31.3 cm .12549 .14902 .180392 rg BT 9.1 TL/F2+0 7.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 29.3 Tm (Complaint analysis/classification with)Tj T* (retrieval of relevant complaint/account)Tj T* (context, confidence gate, and)Tj T* (human-in-the-loop decision)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 344.1575 4 cm .12549 .14902 .180392 rg BT 9.1 TL/F2+0 7.1 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 56.6 Tm (The AI summarizes, tags, estimates severity,)Tj T* (and recommends. The original complaint)Tj T* (remains available. An authorized Admin)Tj T* (approves, rejects, or overrides; only the)Tj T* (disciplinary service executes the final human)Tj T* (decision and records the comparison in the)Tj T* (audit trail.)Tj T* ET Q q .792157 .835294 .870588 RG 1 J 1 j .45 w 0 160.5 m 510.2362 160.5 l S 0 0 m 510.2362 0 l S 0 0 m 0 160.5 l S 510.2362 0 m 510.2362 160.5 l S 0 143.4 m 510.2362 143.4 l S 0 71.7 m 510.2362 71.7 l S 170.0787 0 m 170.0787 160.5 l S 340.1575 0 m 340.1575 160.5 l S Q Q q 1 0 0 1 48.51969 482.4969 cm .12549 .14902 .180392 rg BT 12.2 TL/F2+0 8.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 40.1 Tm (Both flows pass through the gateway for authentication, rate limiting, token budgets, model routing,)Tj T* (input/context safeguards, timeout measurement, and 90-day pseudonymous trace retention. They are separated)Tj T* (because the two jobs have fundamentally different risks: rider AI is recommendation-oriented and must be)Tj T* (privacy-minimizing, while Admin AI handles sensitive complaints but may only advise a human decision-maker.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 48.51969 416.4969 cm .12549 .14902 .180392 rg BT 12.2 TL/F2+0 8.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 52.3 Tm (For the rider flow, the concrete safety envelope is: at most five tool calls, 8,000 tokens, eight seconds per)Tj T* (request, 20 requests per rider per hour, a server-side tool allowlist, data-delimited input, consent filtering,)Tj T* (schema and fact validation, and fallback ranking/manual search. For the Admin flow, the concrete safety)Tj T* (envelope is: no warning or suspension without an explicit authorized Admin action, manual review on)Tj T* (failure/timeout/invalid/low-confidence output, preserved original complaint, and an auditable final decision.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 48.51969 398.4969 cm .090196 .196078 .301961 rg BT 13 TL/F3+0 10.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 2.8 Tm (4.2 Why this is the best fit)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 48.51969 346.6969 cm .12549 .14902 .180392 rg BT 12.2 TL/F2+0 8.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 40.1 Tm <546869732064657369676e2075736573204c4c4d20737472656e67746873016e61747572616c2d6c616e677561676520696e746572707265746174696f6e2c206578706c616e6174696f6e2c2073756d6d6172697a6174696f6e2c20616e64>Tj T* <636c617373696669636174696f6e01776974686f7574206772616e74696e6720697420617574686f72697479206f766572206661637473206f722073746174652e20497420697320706172746963756c61726c7920696d706f7274616e74207468617420746865207269646572206167656e74>Tj T* (does not receive private contact/location/chat/complaint data and has no action tool. For both workflows,)Tj T* (deterministic systems remain the source of truth for availability, fare, authorization, and disciplinary state.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 48.51969 305.0969 cm .12549 .14902 .180392 rg BT 12.2 TL/F2+0 8.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 27.9 Tm (Centralizing controls makes the free-tier LLM dependency replaceable and makes abuse/cost controls consistent.)Tj T* (Separating the rider and Admin contexts prevents the sensitive complaint-enforcement workflow from leaking)Tj T* (into a general rider assistant, while avoiding the orchestration burden of a multi-agent system.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 1 1 rg 1 1 1 RG 40.51969 16.11285 514.2351 11.20001 re B Q q Q q Q
